replies.text:
@TheBiakko I stayed at the Marina Bay Sands just because of its status and I really wanted to experience the pool. I was expecting it to be a tourist trap but the pool area was never too packed and didn't feel like I had to rush there each morning to grab a spot. 

Outside of that it was a really nice place, great location but the hotel layout for some things can be a bit confusing, like having to take 3 separate elevators to get to the top floor, and how most of the amenities are located within the Shoppes section of the hotel. Pricey place, but for a once in a lifetime opportunity it was worth it.

Also went to dinner at Skai at the Swissotel which I believe is the highest restaurant within the city and had great views.
